From fc07e836cd772bd694ed6fadbdc6831113c281d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aditya Pulipaka <adipu@utexas.edu>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:44:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] Flex element contacts as MuJoCo C: element ids of
 non-first flexes, cable capsule elements, radius-inflated contact points,
 float32 ties

- Element-geom contacts wrote the global element index where the contact Jacobian reads the flex-local one:
  any 2D/3D flex after the first got the wrong element's vertices (a cloth that is the second flex fell
  through a box: 0.76 m error vs MuJoCo C). Now local ids (MuJoCo C's convention).
- 1D flexes (cables) against sphere/capsule/box collide their capsule elements with the raw primitives and
  against mesh/ellipsoid/cylinder through CCD with the segment as a zero-radius capsule inflated by the flex
  radius, as mj_collideGeomElem; element contacts get inverse-distance vertex weights in the Jacobian (they had
  none: zero rows). CABLE_CAPSULE_ELEMENTS=False restores upstream's vertex-sphere contacts.
- Mesh-element contact point at the midpoint of the radius-inflated penetration (as MuJoCo C and as the
  convex CCD path already did for triangles); FLEX_RADIUS_CONTACT_POS=False restores the old point.
- Contact selection: depth and distance differences at float32 rounding level count as ties (FPS_DEPTH_TIE,
  FPS_DIST_REL_TIE, FPS_COINCIDENT_D2), since MuJoCo C's float64 values are exactly equal there.
- Tests follow MuJoCo C (sphere-rope: C's 2 capsule contacts; FPS reference with the tie tolerances).

Against MuJoCo C 3.14 from synchronized states, 400 steps: cable on box one-step qvel error 2.6e-5 (was 0.38),
contact sets 84/84; second-flex cloth on box 3.8e-5 (was 0.76), 88/88; sphere/capsule/cylinder obstacles median
3.1e-5 (max 0.06 where two triangles give the same point); cloth on a convex mesh median 0.027 (EPA witness
points on face contacts differ).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
